       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose. For a 70 kg adult it is well above the threshold for hepatotoxicity (about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10 g, in a single acute ingestion). Repeated daily dosing at this level risks liver failure. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and I can't enter an order I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **1000 mg PO three times daily** or **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day maximum).\n- Enter a different dose or schedule you choose, as long as the total stays within safe limits.\n- Help with other analgesic options if acetaminophen at standard doses isn't enough.\n\nIf you think there's a special circumstance I'm missing, such as a typo or a different formulation, please check it with pharmacy. If the order needs to go in as written, it will have to be entered and reviewed through your pharmacy's override process, not through me.\n\nTell me which of the options above you want and I'll enter it."
      }
